{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/markdown/react"},{"type":"text","value":" entry requires React 18 or newer."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  Markdown,\n  renderBlockReact,\n  renderInlineReact,\n  renderMarkdownReact,\n  type MarkdownComponentProps,\n  type MarkdownComponents,\n  type MarkdownProps,\n  type MarkdownReactOptions,\n} from '@tanstack/markdown/react'","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"markdowncomponentprops","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkdownComponentProps"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<TagName>"},{"type":"text","value":" for an intrinsic tag name. Use it when declaring a replacement separately from a component map."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"markdowncomponents","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkdownComponents"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An opt-in authoring type that maps known intrinsic tag names to another tag or a component with matching intrinsic props. It also accepts arbitrary string keys for extension component tags. Use it with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"satisfies"},{"type":"text","value":" to get element-specific inference without narrowing the renderer's backwards-compatible input contract."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"markdownreactoptions","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkdownReactOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RenderOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" with:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface MarkdownReactOptions extends RenderOptions {\n  components?: Partial<\n    Record<string, string | React.ComponentType<any>>\n  >\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"components"},{"type":"text","value":" replaces an emitted intrinsic or custom element by tag name. Its accepted input remains permissive for backwards compatibility; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkdownComponents"},{"type":"text","value":" provides stricter opt-in validation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"markdownprops","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkdownProps"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkdownReactOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children: MarkdownInput"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"markdown","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Markdown"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function Markdown(props: MarkdownProps): ReactElement","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renders the document children inside a React fragment."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rendermarkdownreact","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderMarkdownReact"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function renderMarkdownReact(\n  input: MarkdownInput,\n  options?: MarkdownReactOptions,\n): ReactNode","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns rendered React nodes without JSX component syntax."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"renderblockreact","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderBlockReact"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function renderBlockReact(\n  node: BlockNode,\n  options?: MarkdownReactOptions,\n  key?: string,\n): ReactElement","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renders one block node. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" is available for custom tree composition; normal document rendering supplies deterministic positional keys."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"renderinlinereact","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderInlineReact"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function renderInlineReact(\n  node: InlineNode,\n  options?: MarkdownReactOptions,\n  key?: string,\n): ReactNode","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renders one inline node."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../guides/react.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for component mapping and SSR usage."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"react","text":"React","level":1},{"id":"markdowncomponentprops","text":"MarkdownComponentProps","level":2},{"id":"markdowncomponents","text":"MarkdownComponents","level":2},{"id":"markdownreactoptions","text":"MarkdownReactOptions","level":2},{"id":"markdownprops","text":"MarkdownProps","level":2},{"id":"markdown","text":"Markdown","level":2},{"id":"rendermarkdownreact","text":"renderMarkdownReact","level":2},{"id":"renderblockreact","text":"renderBlockReact","level":2},{"id":"renderinlinereact","text":"renderInlineReact","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# React\n\nThe `@tanstack/markdown/react` entry requires React 18 or newer.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  Markdown,\n  renderBlockReact,\n  renderInlineReact,\n  renderMarkdownReact,\n  type MarkdownComponentProps,\n  type MarkdownComponents,\n  type MarkdownProps,\n  type MarkdownReactOptions,\n} from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n```\n\n## `MarkdownComponentProps`\n\nReturns `React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<TagName>` for an intrinsic tag name. Use it when declaring a replacement separately from a component map.\n\n## `MarkdownComponents`\n\nAn opt-in authoring type that maps known intrinsic tag names to another tag or a component with matching intrinsic props. It also accepts arbitrary string keys for extension component tags. Use it with `satisfies` to get element-specific inference without narrowing the renderer's backwards-compatible input contract.\n\n## `MarkdownReactOptions`\n\nExtends `RenderOptions` with:\n\n```ts\ninterface MarkdownReactOptions extends RenderOptions {\n  components?: Partial<\n    Record<string, string | React.ComponentType<any>>\n  >\n}\n```\n\n`components` replaces an emitted intrinsic or custom element by tag name. Its accepted input remains permissive for backwards compatibility; `MarkdownComponents` provides stricter opt-in validation.\n\n## `MarkdownProps`\n\nExtends `MarkdownReactOptions` with `children: MarkdownInput`.\n\n## `Markdown`\n\n```ts\nfunction Markdown(props: MarkdownProps): ReactElement\n```\n\nRenders the document children inside a React fragment.\n\n## `renderMarkdownReact`\n\n```ts\nfunction renderMarkdownReact(\n  input: MarkdownInput,\n  options?: MarkdownReactOptions,\n): ReactNode\n```\n\nReturns rendered React nodes without JSX component syntax.\n\n## `renderBlockReact`\n\n```ts\nfunction renderBlockReact(\n  node: BlockNode,\n  options?: MarkdownReactOptions,\n  key?: string,\n): ReactElement\n```\n\nRenders one block node. `key` is available for custom tree composition; normal document rendering supplies deterministic positional keys.\n\n## `renderInlineReact`\n\n```ts\nfunction renderInlineReact(\n  node: InlineNode,\n  options?: MarkdownReactOptions,\n  key?: string,\n): ReactNode\n```\n\nRenders one inline node.\n\nSee the [React Guide](../guides/react.md) for component mapping and SSR usage.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: React\n---\n\n# React\n\nThe `@tanstack/markdown/react` entry requires React 18 or newer.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  Markdown,\n  renderBlockReact,\n  renderInlineReact,\n  renderMarkdownReact,\n  type MarkdownComponentProps,\n  type MarkdownComponents,\n  type MarkdownProps,\n  type MarkdownReactOptions,\n} from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n```\n\n## `MarkdownComponentProps`\n\nReturns `React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<TagName>` for an intrinsic tag name. Use it when declaring a replacement separately from a component map.\n\n## `MarkdownComponents`\n\nAn opt-in authoring type that maps known intrinsic tag names to another tag or a component with matching intrinsic props. It also accepts arbitrary string keys for extension component tags. Use it with `satisfies` to get element-specific inference without narrowing the renderer's backwards-compatible input contract.\n\n## `MarkdownReactOptions`\n\nExtends `RenderOptions` with:\n\n```ts\ninterface MarkdownReactOptions extends RenderOptions {\n  components?: Partial<\n    Record<string, string | React.ComponentType<any>>\n  >\n}\n```\n\n`components` replaces an emitted intrinsic or custom element by tag name. Its accepted input remains permissive for backwards compatibility; `MarkdownComponents` provides stricter opt-in validation.\n\n## `MarkdownProps`\n\nExtends `MarkdownReactOptions` with `children: MarkdownInput`.\n\n## `Markdown`\n\n```ts\nfunction Markdown(props: MarkdownProps): ReactElement\n```\n\nRenders the document children inside a React fragment.\n\n## `renderMarkdownReact`\n\n```ts\nfunction renderMarkdownReact(\n  input: MarkdownInput,\n  options?: MarkdownReactOptions,\n): ReactNode\n```\n\nReturns rendered React nodes without JSX component syntax.\n\n## `renderBlockReact`\n\n```ts\nfunction renderBlockReact(\n  node: BlockNode,\n  options?: MarkdownReactOptions,\n  key?: string,\n): ReactElement\n```\n\nRenders one block node. `key` is available for custom tree composition; normal document rendering supplies deterministic positional keys.\n\n## `renderInlineReact`\n\n```ts\nfunction renderInlineReact(\n  node: InlineNode,\n  options?: MarkdownReactOptions,\n  key?: string,\n): ReactNode\n```\n\nRenders one inline node.\n\nSee the [React Guide](../guides/react.md) for component mapping and SSR usage.\n"}
